9) Rollout Plan 🧪➡️✅

Phase 0: Dry-run
	•	Install Expiring Deployments cluster-wide with dryRun=true
	•	Observe logs for 1–2 weeks
	•	Validate allowlist and metadata correctness

Phase 1: Namespace TTL enforcement
	•	Enable real deletion for allowlisted preview namespaces
	•	Keep Helm TTL disabled initially

Phase 2: Helm TTL enforcement
	•	Enable Helm TTL uninstall for shared namespaces that are explicitly allowlisted
	•	Add stronger safeguards (owner annotations, required labels)

Phase 3 (optional): Notifications & metrics
	•	Slack/webhook notifications on cleanup
	•	Prometheus metrics (counts, failures, duration)

⸻

10) Risks & Mitigations 🛡️

Risk: accidental deletion
	•	Mitigation: opt-in annotation required + protected namespaces + dry-run default + allowlist

Risk: Helm uninstall requires broad RBAC
	•	Mitigation: scope to allowlisted namespaces; optionally bind permissions only in managed namespaces; document recommended use in non-prod

Risk: namespaces stuck terminating
	•	Mitigation: detect and log “stuck” namespaces; do not remove finalizers automatically (unless explicitly enabled later)

